<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI33-QA1-WINDOWS-PATH-FAIL>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI33-QA1-WINDOWS-PATH-FAIL" ;
  triage:title "test_run_admission_capacity.py hardcodes POSIX paths, fails just-lint on windows-latest CI" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr's AI33-QA-1 verdict confirmed via windows-latest CI job log (not flaky) that 2 tests in test_run_admission_capacity.py hardcode POSIX-only paths (/tmp/atm, /Users/capacity) at lines 28-30 and 54-61, which break under Windows path semantics. This is a genuine cross-platform CI failure, not a flake." ;
  triage:progressNote "AI33-M5-NINEFIX-QA-1 (2026-07-30): the original POSIX-path hardcoding IS fixed at a8d1e237 -- temp_path() now resolves via Path(tempfile.gettempdir())/name; grep of scripts/smoke/ for '/Users/capacity' and '/tmp/atm' returns zero matches (confirmed by req-qa). HOWEVER `gh pr checks 695 -R randlee/atm-core` at head a8d1e23777616a6b0a6c8c87e99c2dc2b5904a67 shows 'Just lint (windows-latest)' FAILING (run 30509874157, job 90767409974) -- confirmed via job log, not a flake: clippy error 'unused variable: socket_path' plus 'you seem to be trying to use match to destructure a single infallible pattern' in crates/atm-daemon (the new local_ipc_real_daemon_admission_burst_accepts_each_public_write test added by AI33-M5-NO-REAL-DAEMON-CI-TEST's fix). Root cause: crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root/local_ipc.rs:248 clones socket_path unconditionally into a thread closure, but only the #[cfg(not(windows))] branch (274-283) uses it -- under #[cfg(windows)] it is captured-but-unused, and the single-arm match on LocalDaemonConnection::TcpLoopback (266-273) trips clippy's single-infallible-pattern lint. This is a genuine NEW windows-only compile-lint regression introduced by this fix batch, distinct from and additional to the original finding's POSIX-path-literal defect. Test(windows-latest) itself passes (the test never runs on Windows CI because clippy fails first); the windows-latest leg as a whole is red. Remains OPEN -- do not close. Required correction: gate the socket_path clone/use under #[cfg(not(windows))] (or prefix with _ and restructure the match into a let-else) so windows-latest clippy passes." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "cross-platform" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-30T01:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
